          'Probabilities lie between 0 and 1. For independent events P(A and B) = P(A) × P(B). For either event P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B); the subtraction removes the double count. The probability of the complement is 1 − P(A), often the easiest route (“at least one” is one minus “none”). The binomial distribution gives the probability of exactly k successes in n independent trials with success probability p: P(k) = nCk pᵏ (1 − p)ⁿ⁻ᵏ.',
